      "raw_text": "To find out how many socks Lindsay has missed, we need to compare the total number of socks she needs to wash with the number of socks she has actually washed.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of socks Lindsay has washed.**\nLindsay washed 10 pairs of socks and 15 loose socks.\nSince 1 pair equals 2 socks:\n$$10 \\text{ pairs} \\times 2 \\text{ socks/pair} = 20 \\text{ socks}$$\n\nNow, add the loose socks to the socks from the pairs:\n$$20 \\text{ socks (from pairs)} + 15 \\text{ socks (loose)} = 35 \\text{ socks washed}$$\n\n**Step 2: Determine the number of socks missed.**\nThe total number of socks that need washing is 50.\nThe number of socks already washed is 35.\nTo find the missed socks, subtract the washed socks from the total required:\n$$50 \\text{ (total needed)} - 35 \\text{ (washed)} = 15 \\text{ socks missed}$$\n\n#### 15<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "To find out how many socks Lindsay has missed, we need to compare the total number of socks she needs to wash with the number of socks she has actually washed.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of socks Lindsay has washed.**\nLindsay washed 10 pairs of socks and 15 loose socks.\nSince 1 pair equals 2 socks:\n$$10 \\text{ pairs} \\times 2 \\text{ socks/pair} = 20 \\text{ socks}$$\n\nNow, add the loose socks to the socks from the pairs:\n$$20 \\text{ socks (from pairs)} + 15 \\text{ socks (loose)} = 35 \\text{ socks washed}$$\n\n**Step 2: Determine the number of socks missed.**\nThe total number of socks that need washing is 50.\nThe number of socks already washed is 35.\nTo find the missed socks, subtract the washed socks from the total required:\n$$50 \\text{ (total needed)} - 35 \\text{ (washed)} = 15 \\text{ socks missed}$$\n\n#### 15",
